Licensing for benchmarks/
=========================

This directory contains two kinds of material, licensed differently.

1. Work by Intensivate, Inc. -- the harness, the port glue, the workloads,
   the build and run scripts, and the documentation -- is licensed
   under the BSD 2-Clause licence.  Those files carry

       SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause

   and the text is in LICENSES/BSD-2-Clause.txt.

   A permissive licence is deliberate: this suite links Intensivate code
   together with GPL-licensed programs (GCC 2.5.8, Perl 4.036), and a
   GPL-incompatible licence would make the resulting binaries
   non-redistributable.

2. Vendored third-party software keeps its own licence.  Each tree is
   byte-identical to its upstream release apart from removed version-control
   metadata, and each carries its own licence file:

       compiler-gcc/gcc-2.5.8           GPL-2.0-only
       interpreter-perl/perl-4.036      GPL-1.0-or-later OR Artistic-1.0
       interpreter-xlisp/xlisp-plus     MIT
       lattice-bsmbench/BSMBench        BSD-3-Clause plus a citation requirement
       qchem-libcint/libcint            Apache-2.0
       weather-miniweather/miniWeather  BSD-2-Clause

   A few files we wrote are derivatives of GPL-licensed upstreams and carry
   those upstreams' terms rather than BSD-2; they say so in their headers.

Read next:

    LICENSE-AUDIT.md   file-by-file position, third-party notices found
                       inside the upstream trees, and open items
    NOTICE.md          attributions, and the obligations that follow a
                       published performance figure -- BSMBench's citation
                       requirement in particular
    LICENSES/          verbatim licence texts
    REUSE.toml         declarations for files that cannot carry a header

All workloads are original to this suite; no third-party benchmark suite's
material is included.  See PROVENANCE.md.
